xvfb: answer XFree86-VidModeExtension with each screen's size at its vblank rate

Mesa answers glXGetMscRateOML from the VidMode mode line, and Xvfb has no
VidMode, so the call fails on it every time. Chromium's GPU process asks
ANGLE's GL backend for the rate twice a second when idle and every frame
when drawing, and Xlib and ANGLE log a line each time it fails.

- Xvfb builds the server's VidMode extension, and each screen reports one
  mode: its size, at the rate its fake vblank runs at (-fakescreenfps, or
  what _FAKE_SCREEN_MILLIHZ or _FAKE_SCREEN_FPS on the root window sets). A
  GLX client then reads the rate Present paces it at.
- The rate is exact: a dot clock in kHz over totals that make up what 10^6
  the rate in millihertz lacks, so 60 Hz reads as 60/1 and 59.94 Hz as
  2997/50. The horizontal total is whole thousands of pixels and the
  vertical one the fewest lines that then complete the product, which keeps
  the clock under what Mesa's 32-bit arithmetic holds as far as it can.
- Other modes cannot be added or switched to. Gamma is accepted and not
  applied, as on Xwayland, since a client that sets it at startup would die
  of the error.

